1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,063
In 1799, the first president of the United States woke up with a terrible sore throat.

2
00:00:07,413 --> 00:00:13,122
His doctors did what doctors had done for two thousand years. They cut him, and let him bleed.

3
00:00:13,472 --> 00:00:19,693
The idea came from ancient Greece. Illness was blamed on too much of one of your body's four fluids.

4
00:00:20,043 --> 00:00:24,067
Over about twelve hours, they drained around forty percent of his blood.

5
00:00:24,417 --> 00:00:29,575
That night, he died. Many historians think the bleeding made him weaker, and helped kill him.

6
00:00:29,925 --> 00:00:35,843
Today, doctors only remove blood for a handful of rare conditions. And they take a lot less.
